From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:22:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 042/119] fix: DOF 3.0 lens model - highlight energy is split
 once between gather and splat, near opacity weighted by tap density, jitter
 gets a per-frame phase, mask-domain jitter reined in

1. Energy split. The lens-mode gather layers carried each texel whole while the sprite
   deposited its excess on top, so a lamp was drawn at up to 2x its brightness and by an
   amount set by a purely aesthetic threshold. DownscaleDofPS now hands the excess over
   using the sprite's OWN knee (one shared function, CPU and HLSL), per sample before the
   5-tap average, scaled by the sprite's own fade, and only when the splat actually runs.
   base + sprite == the texel by construction.
2. Near-layer opacity. Covering taps were counted as a fraction of the whole reach disc,
   whose radius is the dilated tile MAXIMUM CoC - correct only when the foreground's own
   CoC equals it. The numerator now carries (R / c_i)^2, so an object blurred less than the
   tile max no longer composites in too transparent.
3. Jitter. The per-pixel-only pattern was fixed-pattern noise, which is exactly what TSAA
   cannot average away. Both IGN lanes take a per-frame golden-ratio phase from the frame
   counter in vDofLensModel2.z. r_DepthOfFieldLensModelJitter 2 freezes it for debugging.
4. Mask domain. g_Taps[].z is the bounding circle there, so the shader's clamp cannot hold
   a tap inside a mask silhouette; the CPU quarters the amplitude and the [DOF] kernel line
   says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
